    "The three real records use auto-dense because their camera graphs are highly connected. All original pose variables and finite sparse observations remain in the problem; admission counts and marginal variances agree with the raised-budget baseline.",
    "Compact cross blocks reduce stored scalar cross terms by 3.39x to 13.39x. Measured whole-process peak RSS is lower, but these single real-record solve times are higher than the baseline. No universal speedup is claimed.",
    "The 128-view synthetic local-overlap graph uses 761 pose parameters and exact selected covariance. It compares zero-iteration linearization/covariance, not full convergence. Its 1500 points are not admitted under the conservative uncertainty gate in either version; no finite geometry improvement is claimed.",
    "The mathematically sparse inverse is selected, not a sparsified covariance approximation. All covariance claims remain local robust Gaussian under fixed K, noise, inlier ownership and the stated gauge."
